Fonts for excali
===============

Font files in this directory (and its subdirectories) are registered
with the font backend when excali-text.el loads, before any text is
measured.  They are not committed: `make fonts` downloads them.

    make fonts        # needs curl and network access

What `make fonts` does (fonts/excali-fetch-fonts.el):

- Lists packages/excalidraw/fonts/<Dir> of excalidraw/excalidraw@master
  through the GitHub contents API and downloads every .woff2 in
  Excalifont, Nunito, Lilita, ComicShanns, Liberation, Cascadia, Virgil.
- Downloads the complete Xiaolai-Regular.ttf from the latest release of
  lxgw/kose-font (upstream Excalidraw only ships 208 CJK subsets).
- If `woff2_decompress` is installed (brew/apt package "woff2"), converts
  each WOFF2 to TTF.  If `pyftmerge` (fonttools) is installed too, the
  unicode-range subsets of one family are merged into
  <Dir>/<Dir>-Regular.ttf.

Font backends
-------------

The module registers each file with every backend it was built with and
reports success for the one Pango uses (`M-x excali-font-report` shows
the font map and which fonts actually render each family):

- CoreText (macOS; Homebrew Pango 1.58 uses PangoCairoCoreTextFontMap):
  CTFontManagerRegisterFontsForURL, process scope.  Reads TTF, OTF and
  WOFF2 directly.  Caveat: of several files with the same family name
  (upstream's subsets) only one face is used, so merge the subsets
  (woff2 + fonttools) for full coverage.
- fontconfig (Linux, BSD): FcConfigAppFontAddFile.  FreeType reads WOFF2
  only when built with Brotli; otherwise install woff2 so the files are
  converted to TTF.
- Windows: AddFontResourceEx(FR_PRIVATE) (untested).

After registering, the module drops Pango's default font map so the new
fonts are seen.  Without the files, text falls back to system fonts in
the order given by `excali-font-families` (built-in lists in
src/excali-text.c: the family, Xiaolai for Excalifont, then Helvetica /
Arial / DejaVu Sans, CJK system fonts, and emoji fonts).  Metrics used
for layout (line height, baseline) always come from Excalidraw's
FONT_METADATA for the element's font id, so layout heights match
upstream even with fallback fonts; widths depend on the font actually
used.

Licenses
--------

| Font            | Upstream dir | License                                   |
|-----------------+--------------+-------------------------------------------|
| Excalifont      | Excalifont   | SIL OFL 1.1 (header of Excalifont/index.ts) |
| Nunito          | Nunito       | SIL OFL 1.1 (Google Fonts)                |
| Lilita One      | Lilita       | SIL OFL 1.1 (Google Fonts)                |
| Comic Shanns    | ComicShanns  | MIT (header of ComicShanns/index.ts)      |
| Liberation Sans | Liberation   | SIL OFL 1.1 (Liberation Fonts 2.x)        |
| Cascadia Code   | Cascadia     | SIL OFL 1.1 (microsoft/cascadia-code)     |
| Virgil          | Virgil       | SIL OFL 1.1 (excalidraw/virgil)           |
| Xiaolai         | lxgw/kose-font release | SIL OFL 1.1 (lxgw/kose-font)    |

Helvetica and Segoe UI Emoji are local system fonts upstream and are
never downloaded.  The OFL allows bundling and redistribution with
software as long as the fonts are not sold by themselves and keep their
copyright notices and license.
